      "reply": "**What happens after you approve**\n\n- The Graph stops at the Node that waits for your approval.\n- The system saves a **Checkpoint**. A Checkpoint is a saved record of the Graph state.\n- Your approval is linked to this Checkpoint. So your approval applies only to the task run that is on hold.\n- When the task starts again, the Graph reads the Checkpoint. The Graph continues at the same Node.\n- The next Node then makes the report.\n\n**One important limit**\n\n- The system can crash before or after it writes the report file.\n- A Checkpoint does not guarantee that the report file is written only once.\n- After a crash, you can get two copies of the report file. You must check for this and remove the extra copy yourself.\n\n**Why the earlier message was hard to read**\n\n- It used words such as \"suspended execution\", \"re-entry\", and \"exactly-once guarantee\".\n- Those words describe the same steps above. The words above are the approved names for this task.",
